# Page top spacing

The layout already clears the fixed top bar. `src/app/Layout.module.css` `.childrenContainer` sets:

```css
padding-top: calc(3.5rem + var(--spacing-2) + env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px));
```

A page or section inside that container must not add nav clearance again.

Do not put these on a page wrapper `padding-top`:

- `5rem` or another copy of the navbar height
- `var(--app-banner-height)`
- `env(safe-area-inset-top)`

Start the page like the drinks menu:

```css
padding-top: clamp(0.382rem, 1vw, 0.618rem);
```

The first heading sits in that small gap. Do not add a second top padding on the header.

The bottom bar is already `padding-bottom: var(--mobile-nav-bottom-height)` on `.childrenContainer`. Do not add another safe-area bottom offset on the page.

When a spacing fix is requested, record it here and in `FOLLOW_PATTERNS.md` so the next page follows it.
